  "worked_solution": "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(8,0),$ we have that $r(0)=8i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=8.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=8$ and $\\omega =4\\text{\u00a0rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =8(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u20614t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
